hadiths[156]{hadithnumber,text}:
"809","""Abu Shuraih Al-Adawi said tat when Amr bin Sa'eed was sending troops to Makkah he said to him: 'O Amr! Allow me to tell you what the Messenger of Allah said on the day following the Conquest of Makkah. My ears heard it, my heard understood it thoroughly, and with my own eyes, I saw the Prophet when he - after glorifying and praising Allah - said: ""Indeed Allah, the Most High, made Makkah a sanctuary, it was not made a sanctuary by the people. So it is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood it, nor to cut down its trees. If anybody tries to use the Messenger of Allah to make an excuse for fighting in it, then say to him: 'Indeed Allah permitted His Messenger and He did not permit you.' Allah only allowed it for me for a few hours of one day, and today its sanctity has returned as it was before. So let the one who is present convey to the one who is absent."" Abu Shuraih was asked: ""What was Amr bin Sa'eeds reply to you?"" He said: ""I am more knowledgeable about that than you Abu Shuraih! The Haram does not give protection to a disobedient person, nor a person fleeing for murder, nor fleeing for (Kharbah) lawlessness."""
"810","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Alternate between Hajj and Umrah; for those two remove poverty and sins just as the bellows removes filth from iron, gold, and silver - and there is no reward for Al-Hajj Al-Mabrur except for Paradise."""
"811","Ali narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever has the provisions and the means to convey him to Allah's House and he does not perform Hajj"
"812","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever has the provisions and the means to convey him to Allah's House and he does not perform Hajj, then it does not matter if he dies as a Jew or a Christian. That is because Allah said in His Book: 'And Hajj to the House is a duty that mankind owes to Allah, for whomever is able to bear the journey.'"
"813","""A man came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is it that makes Hajj obligatory?' He said: ""The provisions and a means of conveyance."""
"814","""When Allah revealed: And Hajj to the House is a duty that mankind owes to Allah, for whomever is able to bear the journey. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is that every year?' He remained silent. So they said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is that every year?' He said: 'No. If I had said yes, then it would have been made obligatory.' So Allah revealed: O you who believe! Do not ask about things which, if made plain to you, may cause you trouble."
"815","""The Prophet performed Hajj three times. He performed Hajj twice before his emigration, and he performed one Hajj after he emigrated, and these were accompanied by Umrah. So he drove sixty-three sacrificial animals (Budn) and Ali came from Yemen with the rest of them, among them was a camel of Abu Jahl that has a ring made of silver in its nose. So he (the Messenger of Allah) slaughtered the, and the Messenger of Allah ordered that a piece of each of them be cooked, and he drank from its broth."""
"816","""I said to Anas bin Malik: 'How many times did the Prophet perform Hajj?' He said: 'He performed one Hajj and he performed four Umrah: An Umrah during Dhul-Qa'dah; the Umrah of Al-Hudaibiyah, and Umrah with his Hajj, and an Umrah from Al-Ji'irranah when he divided up the war spoils of Hunain.'"""
"817","""The Messenger of Allah performed four Umrah: The Umrah of Al-Hudaibiyah, a second Umrah the following (year), (which was) the Umrah of Al-Qisas during Dhul-Qa'dah, a third Umrah from Al-Ji'irranah, and the fourth which accompanied his Hajj."""
"818","""When the Prophet wanted to Perform Hajj, he announced it to the people, and they gathered (to accompany him). When he reached Al-Baida he assumed Ihram"""
"819","""Al-Baida the one they lie about regarding the Messenger of Allah. By Allah! The Messenger of Allah did not start the Talbiyah except from near the Masjid, near the tree."""
"820","Anas narrated:""I heard the Prophet saying: (Labbaika Bi'umratin wa Hajjah) 'Here I am for 'Umrah and Hajj"
"821","Anas narrated:""I heard the Prophet saying: (Labbaika Bi'umratin wa Hajjah) 'Here I am for 'Umrah and Hajj.'"""
"822","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal narrated that:He heard Sa'd bin Abi Waqas"
"823","Salim bin Abdullah narrated that :he had heard a man from Ash-Sham asking Abdullah bin Umar about Tamattu after Umrah until Hajj"
"824","He heard Sa'd bin Abi Waqas, and Ad-Dahhak bin Qais while they were mentioning Tamattu after ""Umrah until Hajj. Ad-Dahhak bin Qais said: ""No one does that except one who is ignorant of the order of Allah, Most High."" Sa'd said: ""How horrible is it what you have said O my nephew!"" So Ad-Dahhak (bin Qais) said: ""Indeed Umar bin Al-Khattab has prohibited that."" So Sa'd said: ""The Messenger of Allah did it, and we did it with him."""
"825","he had heard a man from Ash-Sham asking Abdullah bin Umar about Tamattu after Umrah until Hajj, so Abdullah bin Umar said: ""It is lawful."" The man from Ash-Sham said: ""But your father prohibited it."" So Abdullah bin Umar said: ""Is the order to follow my father or is the order (to follow) for the Messenger of Allah?"" The man said: ""Rather it is for the Messenger of Allah."" So he said: ""Indeed the Messenger of Allah did it."""
"826","""The Prophet would say the following for the Talbiyah: ""Labbaik Allahumma labbaik. Labbaik la sharika laka labbaik. Innal-hamda wan-ni;mata laka wal-mulk, la sharika laka."" ('I respond to Your call O Allah! I respond to Your call. You have no partner. I respond to Your call. All praise, thanks and blessings are for You. All sovereignty is for You. And You have no partners with You).'"""
"827","When Ibn Umar would say the talbiyah he would continue saying: ""Labbaik Allahumma labbaik. Labbaik la sharika laka labbaik. Innal-hamda wan-ni`mata laka wal-mulk, la sharika laka"" (I respond to Your call O Allah! I respond to Your call, You have no partner, I respond to You call. All praise, thanks and blessings are for You. And You have no partners with You). He said: ""Abdullah bin Umar would say: 'This is the Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah.' He would himself add the following after the Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah: ""Labbaik labbaika wa-sa'daik, wal-khairuu fi yadaik. Labbaika war-raghba'u ilaika wal-amal"" ('I respond to Your call, and I am obedient to Your orders, all good is in Your Hands. I respond to Your call and the requests and deeds are for You).'"""
"828","Khallad bin As-Sa'ib (bin Khalad) narrated from his father:Who said that the Messenger of Allah said: ""Jibril came to me and ordered me to order my Companions to raise their voices with the Ihlal"
"829","the Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no Muslim who says the Talbiyah except that - on his right and left, until the end f the land, from here to there - the rocks, or trees, or mud say the Talbiyah."""
"830","Ibn Umar narrated that:A man said: ""Where should we begin our Hil (Ihram) O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""The people of Al-Madinah begin their Hil (Ihram) from Dhul-Hulaifah"
"831","Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet made Al-Aqiq the Miqat for the people of the west"
"832","A man said: ""Where should we begin our Hil (Ihram) O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""The people of Al-Madinah begin their Hil (Ihram) from Dhul-Hulaifah, the people from Ash-Sham from Al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn."" And he (Ibn Umar) said: (""And they say:) ""And the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."""
"833","Ibn Abbas narrated that:He heard the Messenger of Allah say: ""If the Muhrim cannot find an Izar"
"834","""A man stood and said 'O Messenger of Allah! What clothing do you command us to wear in Al-Haram?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Do not wear shirts, nor pants, nor burnooses, nor turbans, nor Khuff - unless one does not have any sandals, then let him wear Khuff, but let him cut them below the ankles. And do not wear any cloth that has been touched by saffron or Wars. And the woman in Ihram is not to cover her face, nor wear gloves.'"""
"835","He heard the Messenger of Allah say: ""If the Muhrim cannot find an Izar, then let him wear pants, and if he cannot find sandals, them let him wear Khuff."""
"836","Aishah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""Five are Fawasiq which may be killed in the Haram: the mouse"
"837","Abu Sa'eed narrated that:The Prophet said: ""The Muhrim may kill the wild beast of prey"
"838","the Messenger of Allah said: ""Five are Fawasiq which may be killed in the Haram: the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, the kite, and the barbed dog."""
"839","Nubaih bin Wahb narrated:""Ibn Ma'mar wanted to have his son married. S he sent me to Aban bin Uthman who was the Amir of the (Hajj) season. I went to him and said: 'Your brother wants to marry his son and he would like for you to witness that.' He said: 'I think he is but a crude Bedouin; indeed the Muhrim is not to marry nor have someone married'"" - or he said similarly - then he narrated from Uthman similar in Marfu form (from the Prophet)"
"840","Abu Rafi narrated:""The Messenger of Allah married Maimunah while he was Halal"
"841","""Ibn Ma'mar wanted to have his son married. S he sent me to Aban bin Uthman who was the Amir of the (Hajj) season. I went to him and said: 'Your brother wants to marry his son and he would like for you to witness that.' He said: 'I think he is but a crude Bedouin; indeed the Muhrim is not to marry nor have someone married'"" - or he said similarly - then he narrated from Uthman similar in Marfu form (from the Prophet)."
"842","""The Messenger of Allah married Maimunah while he was Halal, and he stayed with her while he was Halal, and I was the messenger between the two of them."""
"843","(Another chain) that Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet married Maimunah while he was a Muhrim"
"844","Yazid bin Al-Asamm narrated about Maimunah:""The Messenger of Allah married he while he was Halal and he stayed with her while he was Halal. She died in Sarif"
"845","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""The land game is lawful for you while you are in Ihram as long as you did not hunt it - or - it was not hunted for you"
"846","Abu Qatadah narrated that:He was with the Prophet and when he got to one of the roads of Makkah some of the companions were Muhrim and he (Abu Qatadah) was not a Muhrim. So he saw a wild donkey"
"847","The Prophet said: ""The land game is lawful for you while you are in Ihram as long as you did not hunt it - or - it was not hunted for you."""
"848","He was with the Prophet and when he got to one of the roads of Makkah some of the companions were Muhrim and he (Abu Qatadah) was not a Muhrim. So he saw a wild donkey, so he mounted his horse, asked his companions to give him his whip but they refused, so he asked them to give him his spear and they refused. So he (himself) took it and struck the donkey killing it. Some of the Companions of the Prophet ate it and some of them refused. When they caught up to the Prophet they asked him about that and he said: ""It is only food which Allah fed you."""
"849","Abu Hurairah narrated:""We went with the Messenger of Allah during Hajj or Umrah and we encountered a swarm of locusts. We began striking at them with our whips and set our staffs"
"850","As-S'ab bin Jath-thamah informed him that the Messenger of Allah had passed him at Al-Abwa or Bawaddan. He (As-S'ab) gave him a wild donkey but he refused it. When the Messenger of Allah noticed on his face that he was upset, he said: ""We would not refuse you, but we are in Ihram"""
"851","""We went with the Messenger of Allah during Hajj or Umrah and we encountered a swarm of locusts. We began striking at them with our whips and set our staffs, and the Prophet said: ""Eat it, for indeed it is game of the sea."""
"852","""I asked Jabir bin Abdullah: 'Is the hyena game?' He said: 'Yes'"" He said: ""I said: 'Can it be eaten?' He said: 'Yes.'"" He said: ""I said: 'Did the Messenger of Allah say that?' He said: 'Yes.'"""
"853","Ibn Umar narrated:""The Prophet entered Makkah during the daytime"
"854","Al-Muhajir Al-Makki said:Jabir bin Abdulla was asked about a man raising his hands when he sees the House (Ka'bah). So he said: 'We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah and we did it"
"855","Yūsuf ibn ‘Īsā narrated to us: Wakī‘ narrated to us: al-‘Umarī narrated from Nāfi‘ from Ibn ‘Umar (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) entered Makkah during the daytime.

Abū ‘Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan hadīth."
"856","Jabir bin Abdulla was asked about a man raising his hands when he sees the House (Ka'bah). So he said: 'We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah and we did it."""
"857","# Hadith of Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) on the Pilgrimage of the Prophet ﷺ

**Narration Chain:**

Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported:

> When the Prophet of Allāh ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he entered the Sacred Mosque and touched the Black Stone (istalām). Then he proceeded to his right and performed ramal (brisk walking) for three circuits, and walked ordinarily for four circuits. Thereafter he came to the Station of Ibrāhīm (maqām) and recited: **""And take the Station of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer""** (Sūrah al-Baqarah, 125). He ﷺ then performed two rakʿahs of prayer, with the Station between him and the House. After the two rakʿahs, he returned to the Black Stone, touched it, and then departed toward al-Ṣafā — and I believe he recited: **""Indeed, al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allāh""** (Sūrah al-Baqarah, 125).

**Additional Note:**

It is also narrated from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both) in this chapter.

**Authentication:**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *""The ḥadīth of Jābir is a ḥasan (good) and ṣaḥīḥ (sound) ḥadīth. The practice upon this is the position of the people of knowledge.""*

---

**Source:** *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī, Kitāb al-Ḥajj, Bāb al-Tawāf al-Qudūm.*"
"858","""The Prophet performed Raml from the (Black) Stone to the (Black) Stone for three (circuits), and he walked four (circuits)."""
"859","""I was with Ibn Abbas, and Mu'awiyah would not pass any corner without touching it. So Ibn Abbas said to him: 'the Prophet would not touch any besides the Black Stone and the Yemeni corner.' So Mu'awiyah said: 'There is no part of the House that is untouchable.'"""
"860","Az-Zubair bin Arabi narrated:That a man asked Ibn Umar about touching the (Black) Stone"
"861","# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us, Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm, from 'Ābis ibn Rabī'ah, who said:**

""I saw 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — kissing the Black Stone (al-Ḥajar al-Aswad) and saying: 'Indeed, I kiss you, and I know that you are a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing you, I would not have kissed you.'""

He (the narrator) said: ""And in this chapter (there are narrations) from Abū Bakr and Ibn 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with them.""

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""The Hadith of 'Umar is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""

---

**Note:** This narration is recorded in *Sunan al-Tirmidhī* and is also found in *Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī* and *Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim*. It is a well-known narration that underscores the principle of following the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ in acts of worship, even when the wisdom behind the act may not be fully apparent to the individual."
"862","That a man asked Ibn Umar about touching the (Black) Stone, so he said: ""I saw the Prophet touching it and kissing it."" So the man said: ""What is your view if there is a throng (around the Ka'bah) and what is your view if the people overpowered me?"" Ibn Umar said: ""Leave 'What is your view' in Yemen. I saw the Prophet touching it and kissing it."""
"863","""When the Prophet arrived in Makkah, he performed seven (circuits) of Tawaf around the House. Then he came to the Maqam and said:  And take you (people) the Maqam (place) of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. Then he prayed behind the Maqam. Then he came to the (Black) Stone to touch it. Then he said: 'We begin with what Allah began with.' So he began at As-Safa and recited: Indeed As-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the Symbols of Allah."""
"864","""The Messenger of Allah only performed the Sa'i of the House and of As-Safa and Al-Marwah to show his strength to the idolaters."""
"865","""I saw Ibn Umar walking at the place of Sa'i so I said to him: 'Do you walk at the place of Sa'i between As-Safa and Al-Marwah?' He said: 'If I performed Sa'i, then it is because I saw the Messenger of Allah performing Sa'i there, and if I walked, then it is because I have seen the Messenger of Allah walking. And I am an old man.'"""
"866","Ayyub As-Sakhtiyani said:""We considered Abdullah bin Sa'eed bin Jubair to be better than his father"
"867","Jubair bin Mut'im narrated that :the Prophet said: ""O Banu Abd Manaf! Do not prevent anyone from performing Tawaf around this House"
"868","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated to us Ibn Abī ʿUmar, narrated to us Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyyānī, who said:**

""They used to consider ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Jubayr to be more excellent than his father.""

""And ʿAbdullāh had a brother whose name was ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, and he (ʿAbd al-Malik) also narrated (hadith) from him (i.e., from ʿAbdullāh).""

---

**Notes:**

- **ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Jubayr** — a notable figure in the chain of narration, regarded by some scholars as being of greater merit than his own father, Saʿīd ibn Jubayr (may Allah have mercy upon them both), who was himself a highly esteemed Tābiʿī and student of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him).

- **ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Jubayr** — the brother of ʿAbdullāh, who also served as a transmitter of hadith.

- **Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyyānī** — Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah al-Sakhtiyyānī (may Allah have mercy on him), a renowned Imām and trustworthy narrator from Baṣrah.

- **Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah** — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah ibn Maymūn (may Allah have mercy on him), one of the most eminent scholars of hadith from Kūfah."
"869","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father:that he considered it recommended for the two Rak'ah of Tawaf to recite: Say: ""O you disbelievers!"" and: Say: ""He is Allah"
"870","Zaid bin Uthai said:XI asked Ali: ""What is it that you were sent with?"" He said: ""With four things: None will be admitted into Paradise except for the soul that is a Muslim. None is to perform Tawaf around the House while naked. The Muslims and the idolaters will not be gathering (in Makkah) together after this year. And for whomever there is a covenant between him and the Prophet"
"871","that he considered it recommended for the two Rak'ah of Tawaf to recite: Say: ""O you disbelievers!"" and: Say: ""He is Allah, (the) One."""
"872","XI asked Ali: ""What is it that you were sent with?"" He said: ""With four things: None will be admitted into Paradise except for the soul that is a Muslim. None is to perform Tawaf around the House while naked. The Muslims and the idolaters will not be gathering (in Makkah) together after this year. And for whomever there is a covenant between him and the Prophet, then his covenant is (valid) until its term, and for that in which there was no term, then it shall be four months."""
"873","Ibn Umar narrated from Bilal:""The Prophet performed Salat in the interior of the Ka'bah."" And Ibn Abbas said: ""He did not perform Salat in it"
"874","Al-Aswad bin Yazid narrated that:Ibn Az-Zubair said to him: ""Narrated to me from what the Mother of the Believers used to (secretly) inform you about"" - meaning Aishah - so he said: ""She narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Had your people not been still close to the pre-Islamic period of ignorance"
"875","""The Prophet performed Salat in the interior of the Ka'bah."" And Ibn Abbas said: ""He did not perform Salat in it, but he said the Takbir."""
"876","Ibn Az-Zubair said to him: ""Narrated to me from what the Mother of the Believers used to (secretly) inform you about"" - meaning Aishah - so he said: ""She narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Had your people not been still close to the pre-Islamic period of ignorance, then I would demolish the Ka'bah and rebuild it with two doors.'"" He said: ""So when Ibn Az-Zubair came to power he demolished it and rebuilt it with two doors."""
"877","""I wanted to enter the House to perform Salat in it, so the Messenger of Allah took me by the hand and put me in the Hijr, and he said: 'Perform Salat in the Hijri if you want to enter the House. For indeed it is part of the House, but your people considered it insignificant when they built the Ka'bah, so they put it outside the House.'"""
"878","The Messenger of Allah said: ""The Black Stone descended from the Paradise, and it was more white than milk, then it was blackened by the sins of the children of Adam."""
"879","Narrated Qutaybah, narrated Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ, from Rajāʾ Abū Yaḥyā, who said: I heard Musāfiʿ al-Ḥājib say: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say:

""Indeed, the Rukn (the Black Stone corner) and the Maqām (Ibrāhīm) are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. Allah extinguished their light; had He not extinguished their light, they would have illuminated everything between the east and the west.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is also narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr as a mawqūf (a statement attributed to the Companion himself). It is also narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and it is a gharīb (uncommon) hadith."
"880","Aishah said:""We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Shall we build a structure to shade you at Mina? He said: 'No."
"881","Harithah bin Wahb said:""I prayed two Rak'ah with the Prophet at Mina"
"882","Yūsuf ibn ‘Īsā and Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated to us, both saying: Wakī‘ narrated to us, from Isrā’īl, from Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir, from Yūsuf ibn Māhak, from his mother, Musaykah, from ‘Ā’ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), who said:

We said: “O Messenger of Allāh ﷺ, shall we not build for you a structure to provide shade for you at Minā?”

He ﷺ replied: “No. Minā is the halting place of whoever arrives first.”

Abū ‘Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan hadīth."
"883","Aishah narrated:""The Quraish and those who followed their religion - and they were called Al-Hums - would stand at Al-Muzdalifah"
"884","# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us:** Sufyan ibn 'Uyunah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Yazid ibn Shayban, who said:

**""Ibn Murba' al-Ansari came to us while we were standing at the station (al-Mawqif) at a place that 'Amr would keep at a distance from. He said: 'Indeed, I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you. He says: ""Be steadfast upon your rites of Hajj, for you are upon an inheritance from the legacy of Ibrahim (عليه السلام).""'**

He (the narrator) said: **""In this chapter (on this topic), there are narrations from 'Ali (رضي الله عنه), 'Aishah (رضي الله عنها), Jubayr ibn Mut'im, and al-Sharid ibn Suwayd al-Thaqafi.""**

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **""The Hadith of Ibn Murba' al-Ansari is a *Hasan* (good) Hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Ibn 'Uyunah from 'Amr ibn Dinar. Ibn Murba's name is Yazid ibn Murba' al-Ansari, and only this single Hadith is known from him.""**

---

### Key Notes:

- **""كُونُوا عَلَى مَشَاعِرِكُمْ""** — ""Be steadfast upon your rites"" — refers to fulfilling the rituals of Hajj properly and adhering to the stations of worship.
- **""إِرْثٍ مِنْ إِرْثِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ""** — ""an inheritance from the legacy of Ibrahim"" — signifies that the rites of Hajj trace their origin to the practices established by Prophet Ibrahim (عليه السلام).
- The grading of **"
"885","Jabir narrated:""The Prophet hurried through Wadi Muhassir."" Bishr (one of the narrators) added: ""He departed from Jam calmly and he ordered them (the people) to be calm."" And Abu Nu'aim (one of the narrators) added: ""And he ordered them to do the stoning with what was similar to pebbles for Al-Khadhf' And he said: ""Perhaps I will not see you after this year"
"886","Muhammad bin Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Ahmad Az-Zubairi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi'ah, from Zaid bin Ali, from his father, from Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi', from Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) halted at Arafah and said: 'This is Arafah and this is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place.' Then he departed when the sun had set, having mounted Usamah bin Zaid behind him, and he began gesturing with his hand in a manner, while the people were pushing to the right and left. He would turn towards them and say: 'O people, calmness!' Then he came to Jam' (Muzdalifah) and led them in both prayers together. When morning came, he came to Quzah and stood upon it and said: 'This is Quzah, and it is the standing place, and all of Jam' is a standing place.' Then he departed until he reached the valley of Muhassir, and he struck his she-camel so it trotted quickly until it crossed the valley. Then he stopped, having mounted Al-Fadl behind him. Then he went to the Jamrah and stoned it. Then he came to the place of sacrifice and said: 'This is the place of sacrifice, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.' A young girl from Khath'am sought his ruling, saying: 'My father is a very old man, and the obligation of Allah regarding Hajj has become due upon him - would it suffice for me to perform Hajj on his behalf?' He said: 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.'"" He said: ""And he turned the neck of Al-Fadl (away). So Al-Abbas said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you turn the neck of your cousin?' He said: 'I saw a young man and a young woman, and I did not feel safe from Satan regarding them.'"" He said: ""Then a man came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I departed (from Mina to Makkah for Tawaf) before shaving.' He said: 'Shave, or trim, and there is no harm.'"" He said: ""Then another came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before stoning.' He said: 'Stone, and there is no harm.'"" He said: ""Then he came to the House and performed Tawaf around it. Then he came to Zamzam and said: 'O children of Abdul-Muttalib, were it not that the people would overpower you regarding it, I would draw water (from it myself).'""

[Abu Isa said:] There is also a narration on this topic from Jabir.

Abu Isa said: The Hadith of Ali is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. We do not know of it from the Hadith of Ali except through this route, from the Hadith of Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Ayyash. It has been reported by more than one narrator from Ath-Thawri, similar to this.

The practice according to the people of knowledge is upon this - they hold that Zuhr and Asr are to be combined at Arafah during the time of Zuhr. Some of the people of knowledge said: If a man prays in his tent, and does not attend the prayer with the Imam, then if he wishes, he may combine the two prayers just as the Imam did.

He said: And Zaid bin Ali is the son of Husain bin Ali bin Abi Talib, peace be upon him."
"887","""The Prophet hurried through Wadi Muhassir."" Bishr (one of the narrators) added: ""He departed from Jam calmly and he ordered them (the people) to be calm."" And Abu Nu'aim (one of the narrators) added: ""And he ordered them to do the stoning with what was similar to pebbles for Al-Khadhf' And he said: ""Perhaps I will not see you after this year."""
"888","Abdur-Rahman bin Ya'mar narrated that:Some people among the residents of Najd came to the Messenger of Allah while he was at Arafat. They were questioning him"
"889","Muhammad bin Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya bin Sa'eed narrated to us, from Isma'il bin Abi Khalid, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'eed bin Jubair, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, a similar report. Muhammad bin Bashshar said: Yahya said: ""And what is correct is the Hadith of Sufyan.""

[Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali, Abu Ayyub, 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, Jabir, and Usamah bin Zaid.

Abu 'Eisa said: The Hadith of Ibn 'Umar according to the narration of Sufyan is more accurate than the narration of Isma'il bin Abi Khalid, and the Hadith of Sufyan is a Hasan Sahih Hadith.

Abu 'Eisa said: Isra'il narrated this Hadith from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn 'Umar. And the Hadith of Sa'eed bin Jubair from Ibn 'Umar is also a Hasan Sahih Hadith; it was narrated by Salamah bin Kuhail from Sa'eed bin Jubair. As for Abu Ishaq, he narrated it from 'Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn 'Umar.

And that is what is acted upon according to the people of knowledge, because Maghrib prayer is not to be prayed except at Jam', so when he comes to Jam', which is Muzdalifah, he combines the two prayers with a single Iqamah, and he does not pray any voluntary prayer between them. This is what some of the people of knowledge have chosen and adopted, and it is the view of Sufyan Ath-Thawri. Sufyan said: ""And if he wishes, he may pray Maghrib, then eat his evening meal and remove his garments, then give the Iqamah and pray 'Isha.""

And some of the people of knowledge said: He combines Maghrib and 'Isha at Muzdalifah with one Adhan and two Iqamahs; he calls the Adhan for Maghrib, gives the Iqamah, and prays Maghrib, then gives the Iqamah and prays 'Isha. This is the view of Ash-Shafi'i.

Abu 'Eisa said: Isra'il narrated this Hadith from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn 'Umar. And the Hadith of Sa'eed bin Jubair from Ibn 'Umar is also a Hasan Sahih Hadith; it was narrated by Salamah bin Kuhail from Sa'eed bin Jubair. As for Abu Ishaq, he narrated it from 'Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn 'Umar."
"890","Some people among the residents of Najd came to the Messenger of Allah while he was at Arafat. They were questioning him, so he ordered a caller to proclaim: ""The Hajj is Arafah. Whoever came to Jam during the night, before the time of Fajr, then he has attended the Hajj. The days of Mina are three, so whoever hastens (leaving after) two days, then there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, then there is no sin upon him."" Muhammad said: ""Yahya added: 'And he took a companion rider to proclaim it.'"""
"891","Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Messenger of Allah sent me with the Thaqal (load of baggage) during the night from Jam"
"892","""I came to the Messenger of Allah at Al-Muzdalifah when he left for the Salat. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I came from the two mountains of (the tribe of) Tai, wearing out my mount and exhausting myself. By Allah! I did not leave a Habl (sand dune) without stopping on it. So is there Hajj for me?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever attends this Salat of ours, and stays here with us until departing, while he has stood during the night or the day before that at Arafat, then he has completed his Hajj and fulfilled his Tafath.'"""
"893","Jabir narrated:""The Prophet would stone on the Day of An-Nahr during the morning light"
"894","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Al-Mas'udi, from Al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent the weak members of his family ahead, and said: ""Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun has risen.""

Abu 'Eisa said: The Hadith of Ibn 'Abbas is a Hasan Sahih Hadith. The practice on this Hadith among the people of knowledge is that they see no harm in the weak going ahead from Muzdalifah at night to reach Mina. And most of the people of knowledge hold, in accordance with the Hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ), that they should not stone (the Jamrah) until the sun has risen. Some of the people of knowledge permitted stoning it at night, but the practice is upon the Hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ) that they should not stone (it before sunrise). This is the view of Ath-Thawri and Ash-Shafi'i.

Abu 'Eisa said: The Hadith of Ibn 'Abbas, ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me with the baggage,"" is a Sahih Hadith, and it has been reported from him through more than one route. Shu'bah reported this Hadith from Mushash, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from Al-Fadl bin 'Abbas: that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent the weak members of his family ahead from Jam' at night. This is an erroneous Hadith; Mushash erred in it and added in it ""from Al-Fadl bin 'Abbas."" Ibn Jurayj and others reported this Hadith from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, and they did not mention in it ""from Al-Fadl bin 'Abbas."" Mushash was from Basrah, and Shu'bah reported from him."
"895","Amr bin Maimun narrated:""We were halted at Jama when Umar bin Al-Khattab said: 'The idolaters would not depart until the sun had risen and they would say: ""Let the sun shine on Thabir"" and indeed the Messenger of Allah contradicted them.' So Umar departed before the rising of the sun"
"896","Jabir narrated:""I saw the Messenger of Allah stoning the Jimar with what was similar to pebbles for Al-Khadhaf"
"897","""We were halted at Jama when Umar bin Al-Khattab said: 'The idolaters would not depart until the sun had risen and they would say: ""Let the sun shine on Thabir"" and indeed the Messenger of Allah contradicted them.' So Umar departed before the rising of the sun."""
"898","Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet stoned the Jamrah on the Day of An-Nahr while riding"
"899","Ibn Umar narrated:""The Prophet would walk when stoning the Jimar"
"900","Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid narrated:""When Abdullah went to stone Jamrat Al-Aqabah"
"901","Aishah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Stoning the Jimari and Sa'i between As-Safa and Al-Marwah are only done for the establishment of Allah's remembrance"
"902","""When Abdullah went to stone Jamrat Al-Aqabah, he went to the middle of the valley, faced the Ka'bah, and proceeded to stone the Jamrah at its southern wall. Then he stoned with seven pebbles, saying: ""Allahu Akbar"" with each pebble. Then he said: 'By Allah except Whom none is worthy of worship. This is where the one stoned to whom Surat Al-Baqarah was revealed.'"""
"903","Jabir narrated:""We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah during the year of Al-Hudaibiyah: a cow for seven"
"904","""I saw the Prophet stoning the Jimar upon his she-camel; there was no hitting, nor crowding, nor: 'Look out! Look out!'"""
"905","Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet garlanded two sandals and marked the Hadi on the right side at Dhul-Hulaifah"
"906","# Hadith Translation

**Narrated to us al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth and others, one of them said: Narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā, from Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from ʿIlbāʾ ibn Aḥmar, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:**

""We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and the time of the sacrifice (al-Aḍḥā) arrived. We shared in a cow among seven persons and in a camel among ten persons.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a *ḥasan gharīb* (good yet rare) hadith, and it is the ḥadīth of Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid.

---

**Note:** This hadith is found in *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī* and pertains to the permissibility of sharing in sacrificial animals during the festival of Eid al-Aḍḥā, with up to seven participants sharing a cow or ten sharing a camel, based on the Companions' practice with the Prophet ﷺ."
"907","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet (ﷺ) placed two sandals [around the neck of the sacrificial animal as markers] and marked the sacrificial animal with a wound on its right side at Dhul-Hulaifah, and wiped away the blood from it.

[Abu 'Eisa said:] There is also a narration on this topic from Al-Miswar bin Makhramah.

Abu 'Eisa said: The Hadith of Ibn 'Abbas is Hasan Sahih. Abu Hassan Al-A'raj's name is Muslim.

This is acted upon according to the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others; they hold the view of marking [the sacrificial animal by wounding it]. This is the view of Ath-Thawri, Ash-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq.

Abu 'Eisa said: I heard Yusuf bin 'Eisa saying: ""I heard Waki' say, when he narrated this Hadith: 'Do not look to the saying of the people of opinion (Ahl Ar-Ra'i) concerning this matter, for marking [the sacrificial animal] is a Sunnah, and their saying is an innovation.'""

He said: And I heard Abu As-Sa'ib saying: ""We were with Waki', and he said to a man present with him, one of those who look into opinion (Ra'i): 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) marked [his sacrificial animal], yet Abu Hanifah says it is mutilation.'"" The man said: ""It has indeed been narrated from Ibrahim An-Nakha'i that he said: 'Marking is mutilation.'"" He said: ""So I saw Waki' become extremely angry, and he said: 'I tell you that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said [such], and you tell me that Ibrahim said [otherwise]! How deserving you are of being imprisoned and not released until you retract this statement of yours!'"""
"908","Aishah narrated:""I twisted the garlands for all of the Hadi of the Messenger of Allah"
"909","Najiyah Al-Khuza'i (the Companion of the Messenger of Allah) said:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What should be done with the afflicted among the Hadi?' He said: 'Slaughter them"
"910","Anas bin Malik narrated:That the Prophet saw a man driving his Badanah so he said to him: ""Ride it."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! It is a Badanah."" So on the third or fourth time he said to him: ""Ride it. And woe to you"
"911","""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What should be done with the afflicted among the Hadi?' He said: 'Slaughter them, then dip their sandals in their blood, then leave them so that the people can eat them.'"""
"912","That the Prophet saw a man driving his Badanah so he said to him: ""Ride it."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! It is a Badanah."" So on the third or fourth time he said to him: ""Ride it. And woe to you!"""
"913","""When the Messenger of Allah stoned the Jamrah, he slaughtered his sacrifice, then he presented the barber the right side (of his head) and he shaved it, then he gave (the hair) to Abu Talhah. Then he presented the left side to him and he shaved it. Then he said: 'Divide it (the hair) among the people.'"""
"914","The Messenger of Allah said: ""May Allah have mercy upon those who shaved"" saying it one or two times, then he said: ""And those who shortened."""
"915","Abdullah bin Amr narrated:""A man asked the Messenger of Allah: 'I shaved before slaughtering.' So he said: 'Slaughter"
"916","Aishah narrated:""I put perfume with musk in it on the Messenger of Allah before he assumed Ihram"
"917","""A man asked the Messenger of Allah: 'I shaved before slaughtering.' So he said: 'Slaughter, and there is no harm.' Another man asked him: 'I performed the sacrifice before stoning.' He said: 'Stone, and there is no harm.'"""
"918","Ibn Abbas narrated:(that the Prophet): ""Would stop saying the Talbiyah during ""Umrah when he touched the (Black) Stone"
"919","""I was a companion rider with the Messenger of Allah from Jam to Mina. He did not cease saying the Talbiyah until stoning Jamrat Al-Aqabah."""
"920","# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us** — Hushaym narrated to us — from Ibn Abī Laylā — from ʿAṭāʾ — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who raised the Hadith to the Prophet ﷺ, that **he would cease uttering the Talbiyah during the ʿUmrah upon touching (or kissing) the Black Stone (al-Ḥajar al-Aswad).**

He (Abū ʿĪsā) said: **And there are narrations on this subject from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr.**

Abū ʿĪsā said: **The Hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās is a Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic) Hadith.**

**And the practice (al-ʿamal) according to the majority of the people of knowledge is based upon it.** They said: **""The one performing ʿUmrah does not cease the Talbiyah until he touches (or kisses) the Black Stone.""**

And some of them said: **""When he reaches the houses of Makkah, he ceases the Talbiyah.""**

**And the practice is upon the Hadith of the Prophet ﷺ, and this is the position of Sufyān (al-Thawrī), al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq.**

---

### Notes:

- **Talbiyah** (التلبية): The devotional invocation *""Labbayka Allāhumma labbayk...""* recited during the rites of Ḥajj and ʿUmrah.
- **Al-Ḥajar** (الحجر): Refers to the **Black Stone** (al-Ḥajar al-Aswad) embedded in the corner of the Kaʿbah.
- **Istilām** (استلام): The act of touching or kissing the Black Stone.
- **Raising the Hadith** (يرفع"
"921","Narrated by Muḥammad ibn Bashshār, who narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, who narrated from Sufyān, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet ﷺ delayed the Ṭawāf al-Ziyārah (the circumambulation of visit) until the night.

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.

Some scholars have permitted the delay of Ṭawāf al-Ziyārah until the night, while some of them preferred that it be performed on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr). Others have given broader leeway, allowing its delay even until the last days of Minā."
"922","Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah only camped at Al-Abtah because it was easier for his departure"
"923","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:""A woman held a boy of hers up for the Messenger of Allah and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is there Hajj for this one' He said: 'Yes"
"924","As-Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated:""My father took me for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah during the Farewell Hajj"
"925","# Translation of the Hadith

**Jābir ibn 'Abdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrated:**

A woman raised her young child to the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) and said, ""O Messenger of Allāh, is there Hajj for this one?"" He (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) replied, **""Yes, and for you is a reward.""**

He (the narrator) further stated: ""And there are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allāh be pleased with him). The hadith of Jābir is a *gharīb* (uncommon/singular) hadith.""

---

**Notes:**

- This hadith addresses the question of whether the pilgrimage (Hajj) is valid when performed on behalf of a minor child. The Prophet (ṣallallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) affirmed its validity and further informed the mother that she herself would receive reward for facilitating the child's performance of this sacred obligation.
- The hadith is classified as *gharīb* by the compiler, meaning it has a singular chain of narration at one or more points in its *isnād*."
"926","Jabir narrated:""When we performed our Hajj with the Prophet we would say the Talbiyah for the women and we would stone for the boys"
"927","Al-Fadl bin Abbas narrated:""A woman from Khath'am said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My father has lived until Allah has made Hajj obligatory"
"928","Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father who said:""A woman came to the Prophet and said: 'My mother died and she did not perform Hajj should I perform Hajj on her behalf?' He said: 'Yes"
"929","Abu Razin Al-Uqaili narrated:That he went to the Prophet and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My father is an elderly man who is not able to perform Hajj nor Umrah nor undertake a journey.' He said: 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah"
"930","Jabir narrated that:The Prophet was asked about whether Umrah was obligatory? He said: ""No. But if you perform Umrah it is more virtuous"
"931","That he went to the Prophet and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! My father is an elderly man who is not able to perform Hajj nor Umrah nor undertake a journey.' He said: 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah.'"""
"932","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:""Umrah to 'Umrah atones for the sins between them"
"933","Amr bin Aws narrated from Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr:""The Prophet ordered Abdur-RAhman bin Abi Bakr to (accompany) Aishah to perform Umrah from At-Tan'im"
"934","Muharrish Al-Kabi narrated:""The Messenger of Allah left Al-Ji'irranah during the night for Umrah"
"935","Urwah said:Ibn Umar was asked: In which month did the Messenger of Allah perform Umrah? He said: 'During Rajab.' So Aishah said: 'The Messenger of Allah did not perform Umrah except that he was with him - meaning Ibn Umar - and he did not ever perform Umrah in the month of Rajab"
"936","# Hadith Translation

## Text

Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshār, narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muzāḥim ibn Abī Muzāḥim, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from al-Muḥarish al-Kaʿbī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from al-Jiʿrānah at night as a *muʿtamir* (one seeking to perform ʿUmrah), and he entered Makkah at night and completed his ʿUmrah. He then departed that same night and rose the following morning at al-Jiʿrānah as though he had spent the night there. When the sun had passed its zenith the next day, he set forth from the valley of Sarif, joining the road to the route of Jamʿ at the valley of Sarif. It is on account of this that his ʿUmrah remained concealed from the people.

Abū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: This is a *gharīb* ḥasan hadith. We do not know of any other hadith from al-Muḥarish al-Kaʿbī from the Prophet ﷺ besides this one.

---

## Notes

- **al-Jiʿrānah**: A location near Makkah, historically used as a *mīqāt* (station for assuming *iḥrām*).
- **Muʿtamir**: One performing the ʿUmrah (the lesser pilgrimage).
- **al-Jiʿrānah**: A place near Makkah where the Prophet ﷺ distributed the war booty of Hunayn before assuming *iḥrām* for ʿUmrah.
- **Sarif**: A valley located between Makkah and Madinah.
- **Jamʿ**: A reference to the area of Muzdalifah, where pilgrims gather during the Ḥajj.
- **Ḥasan gharīb**: A hadith classified as ""good"" (*ḥasan*) and ""rare/singular"" (*gharīb*), meaning it is transmitted through a unique chain at one or more levels."
"937","Ibn Umar was asked: In which month did the Messenger of Allah perform Umrah? He said: 'During Rajab.' So Aishah said: 'The Messenger of Allah did not perform Umrah except that he was with him - meaning Ibn Umar - and he did not ever perform Umrah in the month of Rajab.'"""
"938","Umm Ma'qil narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Umrah during Ramadan is equal to Hajj"
"939","Ikrimah narrated from Al-Hajjaj bin Amr who narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever suffers a fracture or becomes lame them he (leaves the state of Ihram) and is required to perform another Hajj."" I (Ikrimah) mentioned that to Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas and they said: ""He told the truth"
"940","Ibn Abbas narrated:""Duba'ah bint Az-Zubair came to the prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I want to perform Hajj so should I state a condition?' He said: 'Yes.' She asked: 'So how should I say it?' He said: 'Say; ""Labbaik Allahumma labbaika mahilli minal Ard haithu tahbisuni (I respond to Your call O Allah"
"941","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever suffers a fracture or becomes lame them he (leaves the state of Ihram) and is required to perform another Hajj."" I (Ikrimah) mentioned that to Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas and they said: ""He told the truth."""
"942","""Duba'ah bint Az-Zubair came to the prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I want to perform Hajj so should I state a condition?' He said: 'Yes.' She asked: 'So how should I say it?' He said: 'Say; ""Labbaik Allahumma labbaika mahilli minal Ard haithu tahbisuni (I respond to Your call O Allah, I respond to Your call, I will exit Ihram any where on the earth where You prevent me."""
"943","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', who narrated from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, who informed me from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to reject the practice of stipulating a condition (al-ishtirat) during Hajj, and he would say: ""Is not the Sunnah of your Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, sufficient for you?""**

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi, may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith.**

---

### Scholarly Notes:

- **Al-ishtirāt (الاشتراط):** This refers to the practice of stipulating a condition at the time of entering the state of Ihrām, such as saying, ""O Allah, I shall be released from my Ihrām wherever You prevent me."" The narrator, Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), rejected this practice, holding that the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ was sufficient guidance without the need for such stipulations.

- **The chain of narration (isnād):** This hadith is graded **hasan sahih** by Imam al-Tirmidhi (may Allah have mercy on him), indicating its strong authenticity."
"944","""It was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah that Safiyyah bint Huyai got her menses during the days of Mina, so he said: ""Will she prevent us (from departing)?"" They said: ""She has done (Tawaf) Al-Ifadah/"" So the Messenger of Allah said: ""In that case there is no harm."""
"945","""Whoever performs Hajj to the House, then let the last of their acts be at the House, except for menstruating women. The Messenger of Allah gave them permission (to leave)."" (Sahih Mawquf)"
"946","""I got my menses do the Prophet ordered me to carry out all the rites except for Tawaf around the House."""
"947","(that the Prophet said): ""The women in past-natal bleeding and menses were to perform Ghusl, enter Ihram and carry out all of the rites except for Tawaf around the House, until they becomes clean."""
"948","""I heard the Prophet saying: 'Whoever performs Hajj to this House, or Umrah, then let the last of his acts be at the House'"" So Umar said: ""May your hand be humiliated! You heard this from the Messenger of Allah but did not inform us of it?"""
"949","""The Messenger of Allah performed Qaran for Hajj and Umrah, so he performed one Tawaf for both of them."""
"950","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever assumes Ihram for Hajj and Umrah, then it is acceptable for him to perform one Tawaf and one Sa'I for them both, until he exits Ihram for both of them together."""
"951","Nubaih bin Wahb narrated that :Umar bin Ubaidullah bin Ma'mar was complaining about his eyes while he was a Muhrim. He asked Aban bin Uthman about it and he said: ""Bandage it with some aloes"
"952","""When the Prophet would come home from a battle, or Hajj, or Umrah, when he was it a tract of land or raised area he would say 'Allahu Akbar (Allah is Most Great)' three times, then say: 'La Ilaha illallah Wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-Hamdu wa Huwa ala kulli shai'in qadir. A'ibuna ta'ibun abidun saa'ihuna li Rabbina Hamiduna, Sadaqallahu wa'dahu wa nasara abdahu wa hazamal-ahzab Wahdah. (None has the right to be worshiped but Allah Alone without partners. To Him belongs the sovereignty and to Him belongs the praise, and He has power over all things. We are returning, repenting, worshipping, traveling for our Lord, and we are praising. Allah has told the truth, and kept His promise and helped His worshipper, and routed the confederates, Alone.'"""
"953","""We were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey when he saw a man fall from his camel, his neck was broken and he died, and he was a Muhrim. So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Wash him with water and Sidr, and shroud him in his garments, and do not cover his head. For indeed he will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment saying the Talbiyah.'"""
"954","Abi Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adi narrated from his father:""The Messenger of Allah permitted the camel herders who were in the camp (at Mina) to stone on the Day of An-Nahr then to gather the stoning of two days after the Day of An-Nahr"
"955","The Prophet passed by him while he was at Al-Hudaibiyah, before entering Makkah, and he was a Muhrim. He had lit a fire under a cooking pot and lice were falling all over his face. So he (the Prophet) said: ""Have these lice of yours troubled you?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Shave and feed six of the poor with a Faraq"" and a Faraq is three Sa - ""or fast three days, or slaughter a sacrifice."" Ibn Abi Najih (one of the narrators) said: ""Or slaughter a sheep."""
"956","Ali narrated:""I asked the Messenger of Allah about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar and he said: 'They Day of An-Nahr"
"957","""The Messenger of Allah permitted the camel herders who were in the camp (at Mina) to stone on the Day of An-Nahr then to gather the stoning of two days after the Day of An-Nahr, so that they stoned them during one of them."" Malik said: ""I think that he said about the first of them: 'They they should stone on the day of departure.'"""
"958","Ibn Ubaid bin Umair narrated from his father:""Ibn Umar was clinging on the two corners (in a manner that I had not seen any of the Companions of the Prophet doing) so I said: 'O Abu Abdur-Rahman! You are clinging on the two corners in a manner that I have not seen any of the Companions of the Prophet clining.' So he said: 'I do it because I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: ""Touching them atones for sins."" And I heard him saying: ""Whoever performs Tawaf around this House seven times and he keeps track of it"
"959","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Tawaf around the House is similar to Salat except that you talk during it. So whoever talks in it"
"960","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said about the (Black) Stone: ""By Allah! Allah will raise it on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes by which it sees and a tongue that it speaks with"
"961","""Ibn Umar was clinging on the two corners (in a manner that I had not seen any of the Companions of the Prophet doing) so I said: 'O Abu Abdur-Rahman! You are clinging on the two corners in a manner that I have not seen any of the Companions of the Prophet clining.' So he said: 'I do it because I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: ""Touching them atones for sins."" And I heard him saying: ""Whoever performs Tawaf around this House seven times and he keeps track of it, then it is as if he freed a slave."" And I heard him saying: ""One foot is not put down, nor another raised except that Allah removes a sin from him and records a good merit for him."""
"962","# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn as-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas رضي الله عنهما, that the Prophet ﷺ said:**

*""Circumambulation (Tawaf) around the House (i.e., the Sacred Ka'bah) is like prayer (Salah), except that you speak during it. Therefore, whoever speaks during it, let him not speak except with that which is good (khayr).""*

**Abu 'Isa (at-Tirmidhi) said:** *""This Hadith has also been narrated from Ibn Tawus and others, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas رضي الله عنهما, as a Mawquf (a statement attributed to the Companion rather than to the Prophet ﷺ). We do not know of it being narrated as Marfu' (elevated to the Prophet ﷺ) except through the narration of 'Ata' ibn as-Sa'ib.""*

**He further said:** *""The practice (al-'amal) according to the majority of the people of knowledge is upon this. They deem it mustahab (recommended) that a man not speak during Tawaf except out of necessity, or with the remembrance of Allah the Most High, or with words of knowledge.""*

---

**Note:** This Hadith is recorded in *Sunan at-Tirmidhi* and is also narrated in other collections. The grading of this narration has been discussed by the scholars of Hadith, with some considering it Hasan (good) and others noting the difference of opinion regarding its chain of transmission."
"963","Abdul-Aziz bin Rufai narrated:""I said to Anas bin Malik: 'Narrated something to me that you understand about where the Messenger of Allah performed Zuhr on the Day of Tarwiyah.' He said: 'In Mina.'"" ""I said: 'So where did he pray Asr on the day of departure?' He said: 'In Al-Abtab.' Then he said: 'Do what your leaders do"
"964","Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The believer is not afflicted by the prick of a thorn or what is worse (or greater) than that"
